    "survey": "Glen Park Historic Resources Evaluation (adopted 2011)",
    "source": "glen-park-context-statement",
    "address_as_surveyed": "664–676 Chenery Street",
    "note": "Falls inside the range 664–676 Chenery Street that both photograph captions give for the 1917 Spanish Eclectic commercial building the text places at 664–670; 664, 670 and 676 are three separate parcels, and the assessor dates this one to 1908. Recorded in the reconnaissance survey of 110 parcels but not evaluated individually; buildings the evaluation did not evaluate are treated as potential historical resources pending further project-level study. The evaluation examined the commercial core at Diamond and Chenery as a potential historic district and found it did not qualify; the city's current record puts this parcel in the California Register-eligible Glen Park Center Historic District."
